\description{
Reads a cohort summary's QC in the Cohort view, before any comparison: each sample's quality numbers (cells per mm², median transcripts and genes, transcripts per 100 µm², median cell and nucleus areas, the shares of cells with a nucleus and without a transcript; a nucleus's numbers null where the segmentation records none) with its bundle's run, slide and panel; the samples far out on one (a robust z-score, the median absolute deviation's, of 3.5 or more, and a difference that matters: 20\% for a quantity, 5 points for a share), each with the reason, never passed or failed; the numbers' medians by slide, run and panel; the design draft's samples by batch and group, with what it says of a group confounded with a batch; the pseudobulk's principal components (each sample's scores, each component's share of the variance, over the genes every panel has); and the panels compared. Nothing is corrected for a batch unless the design adjusts for it.
}
